From 3b02caf35d3a3184e59b9ed22fe4ec37ecb75336 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:11:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] ##arch: Sync the USSE and PDS cores with sgxhumation

Copy the clean-room cores again (sgxhumation tools/usse-dis/r2/sync-fork.sh):
- The assembler now writes the operand that emitvcbst and emitvcbvtx
  (source 1) and emitmtest (the source 0 extension bit) do not print the
  way the closed compiler's vertex and state programs do, as immediate 0.
  The text does not show it, so several words assemble from one line; the
  decoder is unchanged. Three new ad tests.
- The core files carry their SPDX licence lines (MIT) and usse.h's header
  comment describes the whole-ISA core.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
